---
title: Apple Cider-Glazed Chicken Thighs
servings: 4
source.author: Thekitchn.com
source.url: https://www.thekitchn.com/apple-cider-glazed-chicken-thighs-22955999#post-recipe-236920001
course: Main dish
prep time: 5 min
cook time: 35 min
nutrition:
  calories: 606 calories
  fat: 45.9 grams fat
  saturated fat: 14.1 grams saturated fat
  carbohydrates: 8.4 grams carbohydrates
  fiber: 0.4 grams fiber
  sugar: 6 grams sugar
  protein: 37.8 grams protein
  sodium: 426.2 milligrams sodium
---

Arrange a rack in the middle of the oven and heat the oven to 350°F.

Smash @garlic cloves{2} and place in a #saucepan{}(small). 
Add @apple cider{1%cup}, @rosemary sprig{1}(fresh), and @Dijon mustard{1/4%tsp}.
Stir and bring to a boil, uncovered, over medium-high heat. 
Boil until reduced to 1/4 cup, ~{15-20%minutes}. 

Meanwhile, start cooking the chicken.

Pat @chicken thighs{2%lb} dry with paper towels, then season with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Heat @vegetable oil{2%tsp} in a large frying pan or cast iron skillet over medium-high heat until it shimmers.
Place the chicken skin-side down, and cook undisturbed until the skin is browned and the chicken releases easily from the pan, adjusting the heat if the skin begins to burn, ~{8-10%minutes}.

When the glaze is ready, whisk in @butter{2%tbsp}(unsalted) until melted, then remove from the heat. 
When the chicken is ready, transfer it to a plate.
Carefully pour off all but 1 tablespoon of the fat in the pan. 
Return the chicken to the pan skin-side up, and spoon the glaze evenly over it.

Transfer the pan to the oven and bake for ~{5%minutes}. 
Spoon some of the glaze in the pan back over the chicken, then continue baking until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165°F, ~{5-10%minutes} more. 
Turn the oven on to broil, and broil until the skin is dark golden brown and the sauce is bubbling, ~{1-2%minutes}.
